1 World Champion at 87 kg, Iran’s " [:a {:href "/athletes/108215"} "Youssef Karami"] ". But form would not hold in this class as all lost early. Karami went out in the first round to " [:a {:href "/athletes/124339"} "Nicolás García"] " of Spain, and García would advance to the final. Lopez lost in the round of 16 to Əzizov, after he was hampered by an ankle injury. But Əzizov lost his quarter-final match to Italy’s " [:a {:href "/athletes/117439"} "Mauro Sarmiento"] ", who then lost to García."] "\n\n" [:p {} "The gold medal eventually went to Argentina’s " [:a {:href "/athletes/123355"} "Sebastian Crismanich"] ", whose only previous major title was the relatively undistinguished 2011 Pan American Games gold medal. Crismanich had a fortunate draw and did not face any major favorites in getting to the final. The final was a defensive struggle, with no score thru two rounds, only to see Crismanich score a decisive kick with 19 seconds remaining, to win 1-0. The bronze medals were shared by Sarmiento and Britain’s " [:a {:href "/athletes/122662"} "Lutalo Muhammad"] ", who had lost in the quarter-finals to García."] "\n"] [:table {:class "table table-striped"} [:thead {} [:tr {} [:th {} "Pos"] [:th {} "Competitor"] [:th {} "NOC"] [:th {}] [:th {}] [:th {}]]] [:tbody {} [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "1"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/123355"} "Sebastián Crismanich"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/ARG"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/ARG.png"}] "ARG"]] [:td {} [:span {:class "Gold"} "Gold"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "2"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/124339"} "Nicolás García"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/ESP"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/ESP.png"}] "ESP"]] [:td {} [:span {:class "Silver"} "Silver"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} 